						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p>Item #: 5965</p> <p>Object Class: Euclid</p> <p>Special Containment Procedures: SCP 5965 is to be kept at site 50 technological storage facility while research into its properties and effects continues. No personnel below level 4 shall not enter SCP 5965 room. Research requisition forms must be signed three weeks prior to the event. Any form of living form that enters the room without special equipment will be consider deceased</p> <p>Description: SCP 5965 is an Apple-II computer that appears brand new even tho it was discovered [REDACTED]</p> <p>SCP 5965 was first brought to the attention of the foundation as a result of a news article that claimed that there was a new machine that can take it to the next step, full immersion virtual reality<br /> As the result of that the machine started having “technical issues” and getting people trapped on the virtual reality who were later claimed on vegetative state only 2 of the [INFORMATION NOT AVAILABLE] survived. it appears that SCP 5965 induces players on a perpetual comma without any power source connected to it</p> <p>SCP 5965 reacts extremely impulsive when a living form enters the containment area</p> <p>It appears that SCP 5965 will remain dormant as long as there isn’t any life form near the SCP</p> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cyberkat233" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6420197&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607504783" alt="CyberKat233" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6420197)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cyberkat233" >CyberKat233</a></span></p> 
