					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Item#:</strong> SCP-5133</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5133 is to be kept in standard humanoid containment in Site-19 (See Paraentomolgy Division's database for dietary info). It has been afforded one digital alarm clock set to the 24-hour clock as an amenity, with the alarm set to 07:00.</p> <p>Items created by SCP-5133's anomalous effects are to be investigated, and, if necessary, confiscated (See Addendum 513301 for list of pre-approved items). SCP-5133 is not to be restrained from wishing for &quot;a good night's sleep&quot; unless for testing purposes approved by the research head of Site-19's Paraentomology Division.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5133 is a 1.6m tall bipedal insectoid entity, structured and patterned similarly to a female convergent lady beetle, <em>(Hippodamia convergens)</em> though it only has 4 limbs. Though wings are present in the subject, they are only vestigial.</p> <p>SCP-5133 has an ability that it has described as &quot;wish fulfillment.&quot; This ability can be used after certain events, the following of which have been observed:</p> <ul> <li>SCP-5133 views a digital clock as it displays 11:11 local time. Event will fail if: <ul> <li>The clock is more than 5 minutes out of sync with satellite time</li> <li>SCP-5133 sees the clock turn from 11:10 to 11:11</li> <li>SCP-5133 sees the clock turn from 11:11 to 11:12</li> <li>SCP-5133 views the clock again after looking away and it still displays 11:11</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <ul> <li>One of the hairs lining SCP-5133's antennae falls off, and SCP-5133 places it onto the end of one of its front limbs and covers its eyes with the other, and then blows air softly in front of itself. Event will fail if the hair still rests on SCP-5133's front limb when it uncovers its eyes.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5133 blows out all candles on a decorated cake in one breath on April 27th.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5133 holds out a seeding white dandelion with one limb, and the other covers its eyes, and it then blows air at the dandelion head. Event will fail if all of the dandelion seeds are not detached from the dandelion head once it uncovers its eyes.</li> </ul> <p>Once an event is completed, SCP-5133 may then make a statement starting with &quot;I wish for,&quot; followed by one item, be it physical or not.</p> <p>If it had requested a physical item, within 5-10 minutes, if SCP-5133 did not specify a time or place for which the item to manifest, the item that SCP-5133 had stated will manifest in a place that is physically accessible to it.</p> <p>Non-physical items requested will also manifest in the same given timeframe, though the means by which they do are inconsistent across instances.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-681490-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Addendum&nbsp;513301:&nbsp;Approved&nbsp;items</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Addendum&nbsp;513301:&nbsp;Approved&nbsp;items</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Request</th> <th>Effect</th> <th>Notes</th> </tr> <tr> <td>&quot;A good night's sleep&quot;</td> <td>SCP-5133 will be able to sleep normally according to its natural circadian rhythm despite its usual problems with insomnia.</td> <td>SCP-5133 will always use its 11:11 wish for this if it can.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>&quot;You all to have lovely birthdays, as well&quot;</td> <td>Research personnel directly involved with the performance of Test 5133-111 on 2018/04/27 reported significantly happy birthdays during the following year.</td> <td>Yearly repitition of this test for consistency in data has been approved by Paraentomology head Marie Vasquez on 2019/02/07.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>&quot;A nice meal&quot;</td> <td>A live larva, unidentified as any known species, with a body .4m thick and 1m long will manifest near SCP-5133. SCP-5133 will eat it alive.</td> <td>SCP-5133 has not commented on what the larva is other than that it is its favorite food.</td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>&#171; <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5132">SCP-5132</a> | SCP-5133 | <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5134">SCP-5134</a> &#187;</p> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/www-yahoo" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3770446&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607504784" alt="www-yahoo" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3770446)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/www-yahoo" >www-yahoo</a></span></p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-681490-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. For example, a request for a concept such as &quot;happiness&quot; will lead to slight fluctuations in circumstance for the benefit of the recipient of said &quot;happiness,&quot; while a wish for &quot;beauty&quot; will simply change the recipient's perception of themself as well as those around them rather than alter anything physically. (See documentation for tests 5133-227 and 5133-077 for more information.)</div> </div> 
